Verdict is a native Swift application. Its model inference runs on MLX through
mlx-swift; no Python runs at runtime. Third-party code linked into the app is
listed, with each licence text, in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt (shipped in
Verdict.app/Contents/Resources next to this file).

Laya inference
--------------
Sources/VerdictEngine/Laya is a Swift port of laya-mlx 0.2.0
(https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-mlx, Apache-2.0): the network (model.py) and
the prompt, question rendering and calibration code (common.py, agent.py).
laya-mlx carries this notice, reproduced as Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires:

    laya-mlx
    Copyright 2026 laya-mlx contributors

    This product includes software derived from Laya:
    https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
    Copyright Convai Innovations and Laya contributors. Licensed under Apache-2.0.
    Upstream source revision: 573e5b62696ba441230cd6be71d593331b5d23af

    The token sequence construction, question rendering, confidence calculation,
    presets, email utilities and language router are adapted from Laya.
    The neural network is reimplemented using Apple's MLX, following Laya's
    DecisionModel and the ModernBERT architecture in Hugging Face Transformers.
    Model weights are downloaded separately from Convai Innovations on Hugging Face;
    they are not included in this repository.

Von inference
-------------
Sources/VerdictEngine/Von is a Swift port of the option-marker backend of
von-sdk 1.1.1 and 1.2.2 (https://github.com/wfzyx/von), Copyright 2026 Victor
Hugo Panisa, Apache-2.0.

Tokenizers
----------
Sources/VerdictEngine/Tokenizer holds Verdict's own byte-level and Metaspace BPE
tokenizers for the catalog models' tokenizer.json files, written from scratch to
give the same token ids as Hugging Face tokenizers (checked against its Rust
implementation on 4,200 fixed texts with no mismatch). A file they do not
recognise falls back to swift-transformers' Tokenizers library.

Models
------
Verdict bundles no model weights. On first use it downloads them from Hugging
Face; each keeps its own licence:

- Laya English, Laya Multilingual and Laya Typed decisions by Convai
  Innovations (https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations), Apache-2.0, in the
  MLX conversions aac6fef/laya-mlx, aac6fef/laya-multilingual-mlx and
  aac6fef/laya-typed-decisions-mlx (each with an Apache-2.0 LICENSE).
- Von 1.1 and Von 1.2 by Victor Hugo Panisa (https://huggingface.co/wfzyx/von),
  pinned revisions d8bb5e0745d8ee1fb65d536d6d4892d54d5a93fd and
  5df8185a4f2327ad0a7cd117cc4f701ac557b9ae; the model card declares
  Apache-2.0.
- Jev by TypeSafe is a hosted API. Verdict does not run or download it; it
  appears only as a measured reference in the benchmark table.

